# Python bytecode from the CI check scripts in .github/scripts/.
# Importing one of them (or pytest touching them) writes __pycache__ next to the
# source, and a `git add -A` then sweeps it in.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Evidence written by the collectors. These used to live only in a local
# .git/info/exclude, which is not committed - so anyone who cloned this repo
# and ran the collector in it could commit a real host's triage output,
# including a hostname, user list and process list from a machine that may be
# under investigation. Ignoring them is part of the tool's read-only promise.
*_20[0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]_*/
tatar.log
summary.json
findings.json
TATAR_Report_*.txt
manifest_sha256.txt
chain_of_custody.txt
binary_hashes.txt

# Editor / OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/
